  property of the root aggregator. Any divergence between this report and its baseline twin would
  therefore be a genuine signal about artifact selection or classpath composition rather than about
  edited code, and it would still owe a register row.

  That makes this module a control on the strategy by which the platform modules the JDK removed were
  reinstated. They were restored as ordinary javax namespace Maven artifacts, declared once in the
  global dependency block of the root aggregator and inherited by every child module, which reproduces
  the ubiquity the former platform library provided and is why no import of this module needed to
  change. Artifact eligibility was decided by inspecting each jar's package prefixes rather than its
  coordinates. This module is the reactor's densest consumer of the removed XML binding API, with
  thirteen consuming files in its main source, more than any other single module.

  Two points are stated precisely, because a loose version of either would mislead a later reader.
  First, the class this report names is a controller over the association model, and that model is
  annotated with the javax persistence API but is not itself among those thirteen binding API
  consumers; the person model that it aggregates, and that the methods below serialise as part of the
  association graph, is one of them. Second, the annotation of this module's data access layer that the
  reinstated annotation API satisfies is the JSR 250 post construct annotation, and not a nullability
  annotation: no nullability annotation of that package appears anywhere in this module, so a failure
  to resolve one would point somewhere other than the reinstatement.

